1
00:00:02,669 --> 00:00:03,545
<i>'Bi?</i>

2
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,547
[BEA] <i>I'll wait for you outside.</i>

3
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:09,217
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [COP GRUNTING]

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:13,430
[CALOY]<i> I knew you couldn't</i>
<i>stay away from me.</i>

5
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>We have a lot of work to do.</i>

6
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:23,064
<i>Happy birthday to me.</i>

7
00:00:23,773 --> 00:00:25,233
[PRECIOUS OVER PHONE]
<i>It's a bit sad.</i>

8
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:27,861
<i>I don't think anyone</i>
<i>remembered my birthday.</i>

9
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:30,697
<i>I did! I remembered it's today!</i>

10
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:33,241
<i>Can I take you out to dinner later?</i>

11
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>You can.</i>

12
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:35,702
<i>Bye.</i>

13
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:37,495
<i>I've fallen in love with Precious.</i>

14
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:40,040
<i>But I promise, at the right time,</i>

15
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:42,167
<i>I'll tell her everything.</i>

16
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:44,586
[BILLY] <i>You know what, dude?</i>

17
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:48,214
<i>I didn't expect Auntie Pres</i>
<i>to find love again</i>

18
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:53,511
<i>after Uncle Rico died</i>
<i>right on their wedding day.</i>

19
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:57,515
<i>I have always admired her</i>
<i>for being so cheerful</i>

20
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,350
<i>despite all our problems.</i>

21
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,105
<i>It's true.</i>

22
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,983
<i>True love transforms you.</i>

23
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:09,569
<i>It makes you whole.</i>

24
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:12,697
<i>It's a different sense of happiness</i>
<i>when someone loves you.</i>

25
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,786
<i>And when you love someone too.</i>

26
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>Listen, Precious…</i>

27
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>Sorry this is so last-minute.</i>

28
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,251
<i>What?</i>

29
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:26,544
<i>- She said yes.</i>
<i>- Okay?</i>

30
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,087
<i>- Yay!</i>
<i>- She's coming here.</i>

31
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:31,341
Do you know who Auntie Pres is dating?

32
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:35,553
[LYDIA] <i>It's Sir Eric.</i>
<i>Your aunt is dating Sir Eric.</i>

33
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:38,056
[BILLY] <i>Eric? As in, the same Sir Eric?</i>

34
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>- Surprise!</i>
<i>- Surprise!</i>

35
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,778
- [PEOPLE CHEERING]
- [PRECIOUS LAUGHS]<i> Billy!</i>

36
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:55,406
[EVERYONE]
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

37
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:59,077
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

38
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,079
[PRECIOUS] Billy, you are
behind all this, aren't you?

39
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:07,168
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday</i>
<i>Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

40
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:11,464
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:39,742
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

42
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:41,870
[PHONE BEEPS]

43
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,001
[PHONE BEEPS]

44
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:54,549
[PHONE BEEPS]

45
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:02,307
[PRECIOUS GASPS]
Billy! Oh my God!

46
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,059
Are you okay?

47
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,687
You know him, Auntie?

48
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:09,105
[PRECIOUS] Uh…

49
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:10,857
Yes. That's Sir Eric.

50
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,735
I was planning to
tell you about him, Billy.

51
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,738
Billy, I can explain.

52
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,990
I didn't plan to hide it from your aunt--

53
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:21,159
You just won't leave us alone.

54
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:23,369
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,872
I only asked for one thing.

56
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:26,873
Billy--

57
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,333
[BILLY] Just leave.

58
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:30,168
Stay away from my family.

59
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:32,003
Billy, what's going on?

60
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,672
How could you be so selfish?

61
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:36,341
Seriously?

62
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:40,929
You even made a fool of the person
who raised us and cared for us

63
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:42,931
when that should have been you?!

64
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:44,849
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

65
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:46,851
He's your father, Billy?

66
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:50,021
I didn't mean to fool anyone.

67
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,441
Precious…

68
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:54,692
Leave.

69
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,611
You're a liar!

70
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:59,364
- Precious…
- I said leave!

71
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,824
Never show your face here again! Leave!

72
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:02,867
Get out!

73
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:04,160
Are you okay?

74
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:08,831
Billy…

75
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:11,834
Dude…

76
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:16,130
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

77
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:24,973
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:07,849
[CRYING] Billy, I'm sorry.

79
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:10,810
- I didn't know.
- Auntie Pres…

80
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:12,729
I really didn't know.

81
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:14,689
[SOBS, SNIFFLES]

82
00:05:14,772 --> 00:05:17,442
I'm sorry too, that you
got dragged into this.

83
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:20,611
I'm really sorry.

84
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:24,407
I'm sorry that my father
is a liar. [SNIFFLES]

85
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:30,913
I was planning to tell you that
we've been going out.

86
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:33,916
I didn't know that the guy
who was nice to me and Oliver

87
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,793
was a huge liar.

88
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:36,961
[SNIFFLES]

89
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:40,798
He deceived me, Billy. He deceived us.

90
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:44,093
He humiliated us in front of everyone!

91
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:45,178
[SNIFFLES]

92
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:54,437
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:54,520 --> 00:06:01,069
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

94
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:22,173
Auntie, you have nothing
to be ashamed of, okay?

95
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,759
You are not at fault.

96
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:33,101
If I could only choose our father,
I would've done it.

97
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,521
[SNIFFLES]

98
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:39,148
Forget about him.

99
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:45,988
Right. You're right, Billy.

100
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:55,414
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

101
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:57,625
[JORDAN] Auntie Pres? Billy?

102
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,294
Are you all right?

103
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,296
We'll take care of everything, okay?

104
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:05,299
We'll tell the guests to go home.

105
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,343
Mm-hmm. Excuse us.

106
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:09,387
Let's go.

107
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:25,319
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

108
00:07:25,403 --> 00:07:27,572
[YOUNG BILLY]<i> Please don't leave us, Dad!</i>

109
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:28,948
<i>Please!</i>

110
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:30,366
[YOUNG BILLY CRYING]

111
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,119
<i>Please! </i>[SOBS]

112
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,496
<i>Mommy, please--</i>

113
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,749
<i>Don't waste your tears on worthless men.</i>

114
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,585
<i>We don't need him.</i>

115
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:43,087
<i>We can live without him.</i>

116
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,929
[SNIFFLES, SOBS]

117
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,723
<i>Please hear me out.</i>

118
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:55,975
<i>I know I did you wrong,</i>

119
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:58,269
<i>but forgive me, dear!</i>

120
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:02,315
<i>Dear, let me explain--</i>

121
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:03,858
<i>That's not necessary.</i>

122
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,861
<i>We're fine now.</i>

123
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:11,741
<i>Just leave.</i>

124
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:15,536
<i>Dear, I'm begging you.</i>

125
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,914
<i>No, I am begging you.</i>

126
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:25,254
<i>Let this be the last time</i>
<i>we see each other.</i>

127
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:28,591
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

128
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:33,804
<i>Dear…</i>

129
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:36,516
<i>Let's talk. Please?</i>

130
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:39,810
<i>We already did. Wasn't that enough?</i>

131
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:42,063
<i>Dear, just please hear me out.</i>

132
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:51,280
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,658
<i>- I can--</i>
<i>- Don't drag us into your mess.</i>

134
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,327
<i>I can explain.</i>

135
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:59,747
<i>Dear, I've made a lot</i>
<i>of bad decisions in my life.</i>

136
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,457
<i>And I want to make them right this time.</i>

137
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:04,418
<i>If you do this again,</i>
<i>I will file a restraining order.</i>

138
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:06,879
<i>I don't want any trouble,</i>

139
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:10,883
<i>but if you drag me into this,</i>
<i>my company, and especially Oliver,</i>

140
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:16,138
<i>I'll find a way</i>
<i>to have your case in Canada reopened.</i>

141
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:20,518
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:25,982
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

143
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:31,696
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:34,532
We're tired of waiting on you, Enrico.

145
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:36,576
Don't test our patience!

146
00:09:37,285 --> 00:09:38,869
I don't care anymore.

147
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,538
You want to beat me up?

148
00:09:40,621 --> 00:09:41,706
Just kill me!

149
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:43,916
Just kill me!

150
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,209
Are you stupid?

151
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:48,796
We can't kill you just yet.
You owe us a huge sum!

152
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:52,049
If you really can't pay
the money back, fine.

153
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,051
I'll get it from your daughter.

154
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:56,971
I saw her at the hospital.
Looks like she's loaded.

155
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:00,349
She can probably pay off your debt.

156
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,561
Don't drag my daughter into this!

157
00:10:04,186 --> 00:10:06,897
- [ENRICO GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

158
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:08,566
- [KICKS LAND]
- [PAINED GROANS]

159
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:12,486
If you dare go anywhere near my children,

160
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:15,197
- I'll kill you!
- [GROANS]

161
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:17,491
Do you understand?!

162
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,869
[WHIMPERS, GROANS IN PAIN]

163
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:25,333
- [ENRICO PANTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,792
[THUG GROANING]

165
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,377
[METAL GATE CREAKS SHUT]

166
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:38,888
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:40,264
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

168
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:10,127
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:20,846
Bea.

170
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:23,808
Criselda is being annoying again.

171
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:26,602
When are you going to pay the rent?

172
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:30,606
I'm telling you,
that woman is testing my patience.

173
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,276
Uh, Ma…

174
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:40,282
[BEA] Don't worry about it, Ma.

175
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:44,245
I'll talk to Criselda.

176
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:45,621
I'll handle it.

177
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:51,544
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

178
00:11:57,633 --> 00:12:04,598
[MUSIC BECOMES UNSETTLING]

179
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:11,939
[MUSIC FADES]

180
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:14,400
[OLIVER SINGING ON VIDEO CALL]
<i>♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

181
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,402
<i>♪ To you ♪</i>

182
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,778
Happy birthday, Auntie!

183
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:19,822
Happy birthday!

184
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:23,325
Thank you, baby. Thank you too, Biboy.

185
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,454
Auntie, was your birthday celebration fun?

186
00:12:26,537 --> 00:12:27,872
Mm-hmm. Yes.

187
00:12:27,955 --> 00:12:30,082
But of course, I miss my baby.

188
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,917
Are you doing okay there?

189
00:12:32,751 --> 00:12:35,004
If you don't feel well
or if there's a problem,

190
00:12:35,087 --> 00:12:36,839
call us right away, okay?

191
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:39,925
What about you, Billy? Are you okay?

192
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,218
Mm-hmm.

193
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:43,971
Auntie Pres and I are just a bit tired.

194
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:48,017
Don't forget to put glucose tablets
and candies

195
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:50,019
in your pocket, okay?

196
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:51,979
I know you're doing
a lot of activities there,

197
00:12:52,062 --> 00:12:54,064
but if you're not feeling well,

198
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:56,233
don't be shy to say it.

199
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:57,443
Yes, Billy.

200
00:12:57,526 --> 00:12:59,528
All right then. I'll hang up now.

201
00:12:59,612 --> 00:13:01,155
Thank you. Bye.

202
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:02,323
Good night.

203
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:03,616
Love you.

204
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:10,956
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,708
Are you really okay?

206
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:18,380
What if Oliver sees the video,
Auntie Pres?

207
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:23,344
I can't believe Sir Er-- Enrico did that.

208
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:25,763
He even dragged Oliver's school into this.

209
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:32,102
I've sent an email to the school
and asked them to fire him

210
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:35,147
to make sure this won't happen again.

211
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,691
I'll also go there myself to check.

212
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:40,945
What if he keeps bothering you?

213
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:44,323
What if he becomes more desperate?

214
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:47,618
What if he tells Oliver the truth?

215
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:53,290
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:56,043
I don't want him to find out
from someone else.

217
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:04,969
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,934
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

219
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,487
[BAGS THUD]

220
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:27,741
Auntie, we won Best Team at the camp.

221
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:30,578
- Wow! That's great!
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:34,456
Oh, and Biboy's father apologized to me

223
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,333
when he picked him up earlier.

224
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,294
Oh. Really?

225
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:41,046
Yes, I was surprised.

226
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,591
I used to see him as feisty.

227
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:46,635
It turns out he's nice.

228
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:50,431
He even wished me luck on
my application to Kingsley.

229
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:53,517
I'm really excited to go to college.

230
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:56,645
Wait. Slow down, okay?

231
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,273
You still have to finish senior high.

232
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:00,983
Let's focus on that first.

233
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:02,359
Yes, I know, Auntie.

234
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:05,404
I'm just really excited
about going to college.

235
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:07,740
Remember what I told you?

236
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:10,951
The first thing I'll do
when I get to the US

237
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,703
is visit Papa's grave.

238
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:19,668
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

239
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:24,465
Oliver,

240
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,425
let's talk.

241
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:32,431
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

242
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:41,065
You know that I love you, right?

243
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:46,987
And that I'd do anything to protect you.

244
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,408
I also know…

245
00:15:55,621 --> 00:16:00,000
that we made a promise
not to lie to each other.

246
00:16:04,505 --> 00:16:09,218
But I broke that promise.

247
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:13,514
What do you mean?

248
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:19,520
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:25,401
You want to study at Kingsley
because of our father, right?

250
00:16:30,572 --> 00:16:33,951
The truth is, he's not buried abroad.

251
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:38,205
It's not true that he's dead.

252
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:45,170
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:48,549
Our father is still alive, Oliver.

254
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,636
He's alive?

255
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:59,351
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,854
I didn't tell you because

257
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,982
he abandoned us,

258
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:06,984
and I didn't want you to get hurt.

259
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:13,157
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,951
Auntie Pres and I love you so much.

261
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,038
Especially me. Right?

262
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:25,419
And I would do anything to protect you.

263
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:31,592
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:38,098
Our father went to Canada.

265
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:41,143
Then,

266
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:44,396
he scammed a lot of people

267
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,023
and was sent to jail.

268
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:52,613
But now, he's back here
in the Philippines.

269
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:58,660
Where is he?

270
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:07,169
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:18,847
You know Sir Eric,
the guy you met at school?

272
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,021
He's our father.

273
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:33,612
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:44,164
But that's not his real name.

275
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:51,547
[MUSIC BECOMES SOMBER]

276
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:53,674
[BILLY] He lied to you and Auntie Pres.

277
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:56,009
But that won't happen again.

278
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:00,013
He won't get near you

279
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:02,432
and fool us ever again.

280
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:09,773
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

281
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,526
[BREATHES SHARPLY, SIGHS]

282
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:16,530
I know this is confusing
and hard to understand.

283
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:18,866
It's hard to accept.

284
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:21,994
But--

285
00:19:22,077 --> 00:19:24,329
I want to talk to him.

286
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,085
I don't want you to get hurt.

287
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:35,716
If you're really protecting me

288
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,926
and you don't want me to get hurt,

289
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,511
why did you lie to me?

290
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,389
And just because you're mad at him,

291
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:45,017
you want me to lose a father?!

292
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:47,060
I don't get it, Billy!

293
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:56,445
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:19:57,946 --> 00:20:04,161
[CRYING, MUMBLING INDISTINCTLY]

295
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:23,680
[JORDAN] <i>Your sister</i>
<i>loves you so much.</i>

296
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:26,225
<i>Of course you would side with Billy.</i>

297
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:27,851
<i>I'm not siding with anyone.</i>

298
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:33,565
<i>Bro Dude, didn't you say</i>
<i>your father left you too?</i>

299
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:38,070
<i>If he came back,</i>
<i>wouldn't you want to talk to him?</i>

300
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:44,493
<i>I deeply regret what I did to</i>
<i>my children and to my wife.</i>

301
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,371
<i>Am I wrong?</i>

302
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:48,455
<i>We're the same.</i>

303
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:50,749
<i>I still can't forgive my dad either.</i>

304
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:53,585
<i>You've got some nerve, coming here!</i>

305
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:54,753
<i>Billy.</i>

306
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,421
<i>Oliver knows the truth.</i>

307
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,966
<i>I also told the school</i>
<i>about your real identity,</i>

308
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:01,051
<i>so you can no longer work there.</i>

309
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:04,429
<i>And you don't have a family</i>
<i>anymore either.</i>

310
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:09,184
<i>Why does he treat us this way?</i>
<i>What are we to him?</i>

311
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,562
<i>Trash?</i>

312
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,315
<i>Just trash.</i>
